{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795289341,"nonce":"d4j7nm5FRT/2X4hZnYW6IfvG7dM=","title":"Explosions, trails, and flares look like volumetric clouds","message":"\u003e Many assets like explosions, flight, flares, etc. should use volumetric clouds. Also implement according to notes.md. Phone HUD does not work because it needs buttons for all the controls, not a keyboard. Gyroscope does not work on phone either. The up down left right keys should not exist, only mouse on desktop or gyro/joystick on phones. Refer to common phone control (landscape only) designs.\n\n**Today.** A burst is a ball that grows, a flare is a small ball, and a plane leaves no trail.\n\n**Outcome.** The effects of a match are clouds with volume: the burst of a missile, the end of a plane, the smoke of a damaged plane, the trail of a missile, and the glow and smoke of a flare. They look right from every side, and they cost little enough for 60 frames a second on an integrated GPU. The WebGL2 client shows a simpler form of the same effects.\n\n**Relates to** issue 755cbcc, which asks for one GPU simulation such as clouds.\n\n**Done when.** Screenshots show each effect, and the browser test still draws 50 frames a second in a match with bursts.\n\nBelongs to the plan, issue 1d9449d.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}